    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d745">

                <pb facs="1202" n="1186" sameAs="frus:frus1951v07p1/pg1186"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Lot 55D128: Black Book, Tab 137: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Commander in Chief, Far East</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Ridgway</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Joint
                        Chiefs of Staff </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret   priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-11-26T21:55:00+09:00">26 November
                            1951—9:55 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>C–58056. HNC–483. “1. At today’s meeting UNC Staff Officers reached agreement
                    with Communist counterparts on location of line of contact. Meeting terminated
                    at 1930 hours.</p>
                <p>“2. Sub-delegations meet tomorrow at 1000 hours to consider line of contact
                    agreed to by Staff Officers. UNC sub-delegation hopes to secure prompt approval
                    by both sides in order to submit matter to a plenary session of main delegations
                    tentatively scheduled for 1100 hours tomorrow, 27 November.</p>
                <p>“3. After approval of military demarcation line, UNC delegation intends to press
                    for immediate consideration of Item 3. Signed Joy.”</p>
            </div>
